# Every variable this service reads, and nothing else.
#
# Rule 9 of docs/ecosystem/03 §2: a repository declares the variables it needs and the deploy
# provides exactly those. `env_file: .env` fan-out — which hands every container the whole estate's
# secrets — is banned, and this file is what makes the alternative possible.
#
# Copy to `.env` for local work. `.env` is gitignored and `.dockerignore`d, and must stay that way.
#
# Every value below is a PLACEHOLDER. Nothing here is a credential, and `src/env.ts` refuses to
# start on a known placeholder rather than booting with one — a placeholder that boots is a
# placeholder that reaches production.

# --- required ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# This service's own database. It reads no other, and CI fails on a second connection string.
ANALYTICS_DATABASE_URL=postgres://analytics:analytics@127.0.0.1:5432/analytics

# Identity's JWKS and issuer, for the read routes. Token verification is the only thing this
# service asks identity for; it dials nobody else, ever.
IDENTITY_JWKS_URL=http://127.0.0.1:4001/.well-known/jwks.json
IDENTITY_ISSUER=http://127.0.0.1:4001

# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# THE PEPPER. THE MOST CONSEQUENTIAL VARIABLE IN THIS ESTATE.
#
# Every other secret answers "can an attacker act as us". This one answers "was the
# pseudonymisation ever real". With the pepper and a candidate user id, an attacker computes a
# lookup key and learns whether that person is in the event store — and, while their salt still
# exists, recovers their entire behavioural history for the four hundred days it is retained.
#
# WHERE IT LIVES: this process's memory, and the deploy's secret store. Nowhere else. It is never
# written to this service's database (there is no pepper column and there will not be one), never
# logged, never returned by a route, and never baked into an image layer.
# 13-operational-model.md:597 requires it to be absent from any backup that also contains the
# identity database — keeping it out of this database is the strongest form of that available to a
# service that owns exactly one.
#
# ROTATING IT IS NOT A DEPLOY, IT IS AN AMNESIA. Every existing lookup key becomes unreachable, so
# every returning person is minted a NEW pseudonym and their history splits in two. There is no
# re-keying path, because re-keying would require the raw subjects — which this service does not
# have, by design. Rotate only in response to disclosure, and expect every longitudinal metric to
# restart from that day.
#
# Generate one: openssl rand -hex 32
# At least 32 characters — eight more than the estate's usual 24, because this is the value whose
# disclosure retroactively undoes four hundred days of privacy. Leaving CHANGE_ME here is refused
# at boot, deliberately.
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
ANALYTICS_PSEUDONYM_KEY=CHANGE_ME

# The credential Prometheus presents in `x-analytics-token` to reach /metrics. A static token
# rather than a JWT, because Prometheus cannot mint one and identity being down is exactly when
# somebody wants this page. It is worth gating: /metrics publishes which producers are being
# refused and at what rate, which is a map of where the estate's privacy discipline is weakest.
# Generate one: openssl rand -base64 32     At least 24 characters.
ANALYTICS_TOKEN=CHANGE_ME

# Delivery-signature secrets for the event-bus inbox, NEWEST FIRST, comma-separated.
#
# A list rather than one value so that a rotation is a WINDOW rather than an instant: publish a new
# secret, accept both for a while, then drop the old one. One value here would make every rotation
# an estate-wide synchronised deploy. Each entry must be at least 24 characters, and two identical
# entries are refused — a rotation that did not rotate.
#
# This is not the same thing as the service token. The token says WHO is calling; the signature
# says the BODY was not altered between the producer's outbox and this handler. Neither implies the
# other, and both are required.
ANALYTICS_DELIVERY_SECRETS=CHANGE_ME,CHANGE_ME_PREVIOUS

# --- optional, with the defaults shown -----------------------------------------------------------

PORT=4023
NODE_ENV=development
LOG_LEVEL=info
# ANALYTICS_DATABASE_POOL_MAX=10

# Names this replica in jobs.locked_by. Defaults to the hostname, which is the container id under
# compose and the pod name under Kubernetes.
# INSTANCE_ID=

# The image tag, reported on every log line.
# CLOUDSFORGE_TAG=dev

# --- the minimum cohort --------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# No count derived from fewer distinct subjects than this is returned — not rounded, not as a
# range, not "fewer than five". An aggregate over few people is a disclosure, and a cohort of one
# is that person.
#
# THIS IS A FLOOR, NOT A DEFAULT. The deploy may RAISE it. `env.ts` REFUSES to start on a value
# below 5 rather than clamping it, because a suppression threshold that can be set to 1 is not a
# suppression threshold, it is a suggestion — and this is the one number that stands between a
# person and being the only member of a published cohort. See the README for why five.
# ANALYTICS_MIN_COHORT=5

# --- retention ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Enforced by a leased job that runs hourly, not by a policy in a document. `jobs.test.ts` plants a
# row past the horizon and asserts it is deleted — and asserts a row inside the horizon survives,
# because a sweep that deletes everything also passes a test that only checks the first half.
#
# Rollups outlive the events they were computed from, and boot REFUSES the inversion: a rollup that
# expired first would throw away the cheap summary while keeping the expensive raw rows.
# ANALYTICS_EVENT_RETENTION_DAYS=400
# ANALYTICS_ROLLUP_RETENTION_DAYS=1200
# ANALYTICS_INBOX_RETENTION_DAYS=30
# ANALYTICS_IDEMPOTENCY_TTL_DAYS=30

# How many weeks wide the retention heatmap is. Metric 18 says twelve.
# ANALYTICS_COHORT_WEEKS=12

# --- not read by this service ----------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT and the rest of OTEL_* are read by the OpenTelemetry SDK loaded ahead
# of the process, not by src/env.ts. They belong in the deploy, not here.
#
# ANALYTICS_TEST_DATABASE_URL is read only by the test suite, and only when its name contains
# "test" — the database-backed tests truncate. CI exports it; a different spelling would silently
# skip them and turn the workflow's skip guard into the false-green it exists to prevent.
